.SH NAME
et\-user\-restore \- restore EmComm Tools user data from a backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-user\-restore\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-user\-restore\f[R] restores EmComm Tools user data from a
backup archive created by \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R].
.PP
The tool searches the user\(cqs home directory and mounted USB media
under \f[CR]/media\f[R] for backup archives.
Matching files are presented in an interactive menu.
.PP
Use the arrow keys to select a backup and press Enter to restore its
contents to the current user\(cqs home directory.
.PP
The restore process extracts the selected archive and reports whether
the operation succeeded or failed.
.SH RESTORE PROCEDURE
To restore user data from a backup:
.IP "1." 3
Connect the USB drive containing the backup, if applicable.
.IP "2." 3
Run \f[B]et\-user\-restore\f[R].
.IP "3." 3
Select the desired backup archive from the list.
.IP "4." 3
Press Enter to begin the restore process.
.IP "5." 3
Verify that the restore completed successfully.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-user\-restore
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-user\-restore\f[R] after reinstalling EmComm Tools, moving
to another computer, or recovering previously backed\-up user data.
.SH RESTORE RECOMMENDATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Restore user data after installing a new EmComm Tools release.
.IP \(bu 2
Close any running EmComm Tools applications before restoring.
.IP \(bu 2
Restart the desired operating mode after restoring user data.
.IP \(bu 2
Existing files with matching paths may be overwritten during
restoration.
Back up any important data before proceeding.
.SH FILES
.TP
**etc\-user\-backup\-*.tar.gz**
Backup archives created by \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R].
The filename includes the hostname and date of the original backup.
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/ \f[R]
The destination for restored user data.
